Fatio reads the interoperable text and page filenames produced by 禾高子 manualExport.ts.

Runtime dependencies and their individual licenses are installed by npm:
twitter-text (Apache-2.0), twitter-api-v2 (Apache-2.0), lucide-static (ISC, including upstream Feather attribution).
Electron and Playwright are used with their own LICENSE files. See node_modules and the pinned package-lock.json.

JAStudio 1.1 interoperates with the installed CreatorHub local API and database,
DouyinDataReview's collector API and archive, Easel project manifests, and YiMei CSV reports.
Third-party desktop programs and their account sessions are not bundled. CSV parsing uses csv-parse (MIT).

JAStudio 1.2 uses its own Electron account partitions, media queue, creator-page adapters and works database.
Legacy file-format readers are optional migration features. No companion desktop app or developer services are required.
The installer redistributes the pinned Electron runtime, its Chromium notices and the production npm dependencies with their licenses.

