JAStudio 1.5 includes Microsoft.Web.WebView2 1.0.3537.50 for its Windows Channels window.
The redistributed SDK libraries and loader are accompanied by their Microsoft license
in resources/channels-host/LICENSE.txt. The installer includes Microsoft's signed
Evergreen WebView2 bootstrapper for Windows machines missing the runtime.

Fatio 1.12 adopts the user-approved original mainspring logo. Build-only tools
@napi-rs/canvas (MIT) and rcedit (MIT) generate icons and Windows executable resources;
they are not bundled as runtime dependencies. Historical JAStudio version names above
identify the releases in which the corresponding third-party components were introduced.

The publishing calendar and platform rule pre-check follow the design of AiToEarn
(https://github.com/yikart/AiToEarn, Copyright (c) yikart, MIT License). ui/rules.js adapts the
per-platform contentLimits / mediaRules values from aitoearn-server; no AiToEarn source files are bundled.
ui/calendar-data.js holds lunar month starts and solar terms for 2025-2030 precomputed with
lunar-javascript (MIT); the library itself is not bundled.
